# lowpoly-cutaway-explainer fix log

## epoch 0 (2026-11-26): created from a reference reel
Made by Claude from the rea-video breakdown of references/ps1-cutaway.mp4 (43.3 s, a three.js low-poly reel: an animal host in a suit teaches six rules for its own PS1 look, demonstrating each on itself, then three example cutaways on plain coloured backdrops and a recipe board), see reference-lab/refs/ps1-cutaway (survey, review and style aspect by Claude) and reference-lab/runs/ps1-cutaway/look (frames read at full size).
User directions (the reference's own six rules): 1) about 300 triangles, flat shading 2) 64-pixel textures painted by code 3) render at 270 x 480, no smoothing 4) snap vertices to a grid 5) whenever explaining, slice it open and label one part 6) a new pose on every sentence. Brief: "explain an air conditioner".
What was taken from the reference:
- Look: real 3D at 270 x 480 blown up 4x (hard pixels, measured grid about 210 at 720 wide), flat-shaded faceted models, tiny code-painted textures (fabric speckle, planks, grass tufts), dithered banded sky with pixel clouds, backyard with picket fence and pines; studio backdrops in one hue per subject for the examples; the slice signature (halves slide apart, cut face deep violet L 0.17 with orange triangle edges, one yellow outlined label with an orange leader). Colours measured with oklch_colours.py: grass L 0.67 to 0.73 C 0.15 h 128, sky L 0.68 C 0.12 h 265 to pink, wood L 0.53 to 0.63 h 50 to 65, suit L 0.68 C 0.15 h 70, tie L 0.58 C 0.20 h 30, backdrops L 0.47 to 0.78 C 0.07 to 0.12.
- Structure: promise with a count, the wrong default knocked down ("Ew"), numbered steps each demonstrated at once with a "k/N" header top left, a payoff, a callback; one-word captions; the host speaks in the first person, a new pose per sentence; voice young male, quick (2.4 to 3.1 words/s); music 172 bpm (86 half time), dings on step numbers.
- Not taken (do not copy): the raccoon, the yellow suit with a red striped tie, the backyard as is, the topic (making low-poly videos), the rule texts, the example subjects, the watermark, the CTA.
Engine work this template needed (user approved a new mode, 2026-11-26):
- New "renderer: lowpoly" mode: engine/stage3d_lowpoly.js (new file; the toon 3D stage is untouched). 270 x 480 WebGL render without antialias, painted sky underneath, 15-bit colour with a 4 x 4 Bayer dither, nearest 4x upscale; MeshLambert flatShading on non-indexed geometry; vertex snap to the 270 x 480 grid in the vertex shader; 64 px CanvasTextures (13 patterns or an M3 paint function) with nearest sampling; the part kit k.box/cyl/cone/ball/lathe/prism/pipe/screen/named with name + inner; the slice (two clipped copies of the casing slide apart; back faces of the cut drawn in "cut" with "edge" triangle edges from barycentric coordinates); h.d3.label (one leader label on a named part), h.d3.part, h.d3.sentences; a low-poly animal host of 329 triangles built from look3d (ears, snout, tail, stripe, mask, 64 px face texture with 8 expressions, mouth moved by the narration) with 19 poses on a two-bone arm IK and a pose schedule; sets outdoor / studio / room; cameras wide / host / face / subject / part / free framed into the picture band; checks: host inside a subject, subject off frame, and a new pose on every sentence (stage_asset.html validateShot); a cast sheet with poses and sliced subjects.
- asset_reel.mjs: LPMODE, planLpErrors (set specs, one host with look3d, 1 or 2 subjects with size and inside parts), d3Data mode, the low-poly kit API text, sentences per shot for the shot step, prompts plan3dlp / draw3dlp / shot3dlp. stage_asset.html: no neutral camera drift in low-poly reels, 3D setup before the kit is compiled. lib.mjs: the new file on the stage's network allowlist.

## epoch 1 (2026-11-26): fixes after reviewing the epoch-0 reel (reels/aircon-lp-e1-v1, first cut only: 41.9 s, 7 shots; MiniMax about $0.10 in the last of three attempts)
Run notes: the first attempt lost 4 plan tries to background names (the rejection never listed the valid names); the second stopped when ElevenLabs answered "quota_exceeded" (0 credits), so this cut is voiced by HeyGen lucian (free) with the narrator set to lucian in the work checkpoints; the director round's v2 died in ffmpeg (0xC0000142) while Claude Code reaped the run for low system memory. Engine fixes from the run: a background named by "id" is taken as its name, and the rejection lists the valid names; the subject's triangle cap is 600 (aim 250 to 450; the inside needs more than the host's 300).
Epoch 0 got right: the whole low-poly mode works end to end (PS1 pixels, flat shading, textures, header "k/N" top left, word captions, a non-raccoon host in a teal suit, room and studio sets, a pose per sentence, every shot validated).
Grade (v1 vs reference): rhythm 0.43, rendering 0.41, colour 0.37; cuts 11.4 vs 26.4 a minute; frame change 0.9 vs 2.7; colours on screen 19 vs 254; detail 3.7 vs 10.8; harmony monochromatic vs complementary.
Flaws seen -> fix:
- The slice never opened in any step: shot code computed the reveal but never passed slice, passed the toon API's options (w, d, h, colour, top, role, sweat, jolt) instead, and drew its own labels as kit.panel plaques with fillText (the base directions' label recipe), one of them on the closed unit in the hook -> engine: h.d3.thing / actor reject unknown options and list the real ones; a label on an inside part of a closed subject is rejected; template check "slice beats: step, payoff" (those shots must reach slice 0.6 and draw an h.d3.label in their second half); in low-poly reels words come only from kit.header and h.d3.label (kit.panel, fillText and strokeText rejected); template and shot prompt say so and that the base label recipe does not apply.
- The host turned its back on the camera (faced the unit behind it) and stood far to the side, tiny -> engine: the host turns at most 50 degrees away from the camera (re-posed); a subject under half the picture in "wide" or "subject" is rejected; template: the presenter layout (host in front of the subject's left corner, overlapping in depth, fill 0.95) and a TALL subject (1.4 to 2.2 m high, the upright version of a wide thing).
- Headers numbered every shot ("1/7", "2/7", "7/7") -> only step shots carry "k/N", k counting steps only.
- Step 3's line opened with "Then" instead of its number; the payoff had no number -> the number word and part name are the first words of a step shot; the payoff states one real figure from the reference.
- One plum tint over every set (19 colours, monochromatic) and faint textures (flat fills 0.58 vs 0.15) -> template: outdoor yard for hook/myth/loop, a light vivid studio (lightness 0.68 to 0.82), at least four hue families; engine: speckle texture twice as dense and stronger, grass denser, the studio floor a tiled grid by default.
- Too few cuts -> a new camera setup on every sentence together with the new pose.

## epoch 2 (2026-11-26): fixes after reviewing the epoch-1 reel (reels/aircon-lp-e2-v2, 39.0 s, 8 shots, $0.108 MiniMax, HeyGen lucian voice, 358 s wall)
Epoch 1's fixes worked: every shot passed every check (no fallback); the slice opens in the step shots on its word, the casing halves slide apart with violet cut faces and orange edges, one yellow label with a leader on the inside part (evaporator, compressor); a tall upright unit (0.75 x 1.8 m) beside a fox host in a teal suit who faces the camera and changes pose every sentence (present, arms_up, wave, shrug, arms_crossed); warm plank room and an orange studio with a tiled floor.
Grade: rhythm 0.22 (was 0.43), rendering 0.25 (0.41), colour 0.28 (0.37); art pixels across 209.8, the same as the reference; colours on screen 65 (19; reference 254); cuts 20 a minute (11; reference 26); still "monochromatic" (every set warm).
Flaws seen -> fix:
- Shot 6 (condenser) opened its slice off the picture and its label pointed out of frame; the check passed because it only measured the slice -> engine: a label whose part is off the picture is rejected.
- Non-step shots still numbered ("2/8", "8/8"); step headers and labels did not match the lines (a "4/4 Expansion device" header and label on a line about outdoor air; an "Evaporator" label on the fan line) -> engine: kit.header reports what it drew, and the shot step rejects a step header that is not k/N with k counting the step shots, and any number on a non-step header; template check "labels: from narration" (every header and label word is said in that shot).
- A label sat on the host's head -> engine: the label moves to the other side or above the host when it would cover it.
- In "part" cameras the host showed as a lone arm cut by the frame edge -> engine: in part and subject cameras a host less than 80% inside the frame is hidden.
- All-warm sets (room wood, orange studio) -> template: the studio hue at least 120 degrees from the hook's set.
- Flat fills still 0.52 (reference 0.15): M3 used tex "plain" on big casing panels -> engine: "plain" carries a faint grain.
- Writer: two step lines still opened with "Then"/no number and the payoff had no figure (not fixed in the engine; template rule stands).

